I've plotted an example from beast2 tutorial (https://taming-the-beast.org/tutorials/FBD-tutorial/) and the same thing happened again. The HPD bars seems 180° rotated. I've also tried to revert the order of the HPD using rev() but it didn't resolved the problem.

beast.tree <- read.beast(file="bearsDivtime_FBD.summary.tre")

p <- ggtree(beast.tree, ladderize=TRUE, color="grey50", size=1) + xlim_tree(50) + theme_tree2() +

  geom_range(range="height_0.95_HPD", color="blue", alpha=0.6, size=2, branch.length = "height_median") +

  geom_text2(aes(subset=!isTip, label=round(height, digits = 3), hjust=-.3, vjust=1.2), size=3) +
  geom_tiplab(size=3) + geom_point2(aes(subset=!is.na <http://is.na>(posterior) & posterior >= 0.95))
p

The input tree and the pdf files are also attached.

Thanks

